<title>SWEDEN: Autoliv says 90 pct owners accept merger.</title>
<headline>Autoliv says 90 pct owners accept merger.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car safety company Autoliv said on Monday that owners holding more than 90 percent of capital and votes had accepted the proposed merger with the car safety unit of U.S. Morton.</p>
<p>It said trade in the merged company's depositary receipts would begin on May 2 on the Stockholm Stock Exchange and its shares would start trade on the New York Stock Exchange on May 1.</p>
</text>
